# BUGS

dns only resolves: it serves no zones and answers no other machine's queries, it asks from no root servers when it has no name server, and it checks no signatures (DNSSEC).
QEMU's restricted network gives no name server, so in the boot tests dns can only fail.
A failure is a code, not Plan 9's error text, so dial(2) says why in the code's words.
A `!` query of cs looks only in the database, never asks dns, and `@`<attr> is taken as <attr>.
cs serves `/net` alone; Plan 9's `-x` for another network's mount point, and its `add`, `ipv4`, `ipv6` and `debug` ctl lines, are not taken.
